<title>SWEDEN: Iceland airport exports 30 pct more freight Sept.</title>
<headline>Iceland airport exports 30 pct more freight Sept.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iceland's civil aviation administration issued on Tuesday the following figures for airport cargo and passenger activity in September at Reykjavik's international airport at Keflavik.</p>
<p>The amount of freight exported through the airport in September this year rose by 30 percent from the same period a year ago.</p>
<p> KEFLAVIK INT'L AIRPORT	    Sept 1996	  Sept 1995</p>
<p> Freight export (in tonnes)	  1,062		 817</p>
<p>	   import			    707		 470</p>
<p> Mail export (in tonnes)		  44		  48</p>
<p>	import				 124		 134</p>
<p> Passengers			     99,291	    89,979</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
</text>
